#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/batch_study.ipynb:170
msgid ""
"``BatchStudy`` by default requires equal number of items in all the "
"dictionaries passed, which can be changed by setting the value of "
"``permutations`` to ``True``. When set ``True``, a cartesian product of all "
"the available items is taken."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/batch_study.ipynb:172
msgid ""
"For example, here we pass 3 models but only 1 parameter value, hence it is "
"necessary to set ``permutations`` to ``True``. Here, the given parameter "
"value is used for all the provided models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/batch_study.ipynb:-1
msgid "[3]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/batch_study.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"# passing parameter_values as a dictionary\n"
"parameter_values = {\"Chen2020\": pybamm.ParameterValues(\"Chen2020\")}\n"
"\n"
"# creating a BatchStudy object and solving the simulation\n"
"batch_study = pybamm.BatchStudy(\n"
"    models=models, parameter_values=parameter_values, permutations=True\n"
")\n"
"batch_study.solve(t_eval=[0, 3600])\n"
"batch_study.plot()"
